  "description": "The proposed development involves the change of use of 16 The Meadow Way, Harrow HA3 7BW to a children’s residential care home (Use Class C2) for up to three children aged 7–18.\n\nThe home will provide long-term therapeutic residential care for children with emotional and behavioural needs, including those with associated conditions such as autism and low to moderate learning disabilities, where those needs can be safely managed within a small, stable and family-style environment.\n\nThe property will retain its domestic layout and residential character, remaining in keeping with the surrounding neighbourhood. No external alterations, signage, commercial activity, or public-facing use are proposed.\n\nThe applicant, St Caspian Care Ltd, currently operates two established children’s homes within Harrow at 10 Christchurch Avenue, HA3 8NE and 57 Weighton Road, HA3 6HY. Both homes are Ofsted registered and rated “Good”, operating within residential settings with minimal impact on the surrounding area.\n\nThe proposed home will operate as a small-scale residential environment with:\n\na maximum of three children at all times\ntypical daytime staffing of three care staff\none to two sleeping-in staff overnight\nstructured therapeutic support delivered through individual care planning and safeguarding procedures\n\nPlacements will be long-term in nature and not emergency placements.\n\nThe home will operate with a stable staffing model using longer day shifts, reducing staff turnover and daily movements. Larger team meetings and training sessions are typically held off-site.\n\nThe property benefits from on-site parking and strong public transport accessibility. Staff are encouraged to use public transport, and children will primarily travel using public transport for school and local activities as part of promoting independence and integration into the community.\n\nSecure cycle storage and refuse storage will be provided within the rear garden beyond a secured side access gate.\n\nThe development seeks to provide high-quality therapeutic residential care within a domestic setting while addressing the identified need for additional local children’s residential provision within Harrow and London.",
